<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!--
      EI_EXPOSE_REP2 excluded, narrowly, for three classes in v2-shortener-service's shortlink
      package (Task #9): ShortLinkCache, ShortLinkService, and ShortLinkController.

      Each stores a constructor-injected Spring collaborator (an ObjectMapper, a
      StringRedisTemplate/RedisOperations, or this project's own service/cache beans) as a
      field — standard Spring dependency injection, not caller-owned mutable state whose
      defensive copying would protect any real invariant. SpotBugs flags this because its
      structural-immutability check is transitive: ShortLinkCache holds a live ObjectMapper and
      a live Redis client (both fundamentally mutable, stateful framework objects — there is no
      immutable variant to switch to, and "copying" either would defeat the point of injecting
      them), so ShortLinkCache itself can never be proven immutable, and neither can anything
      that in turn stores a ShortLinkCache (ShortLinkService), or stores that
      (ShortLinkController). See AI_USAGE_LOG.md for the specific finding this addresses.

      This is a genuinely different situation from PR #20's RabbitTemplate -> AmqpTemplate fix,
      or from this same PR's CachedShortLink/CreateUrlRequest fix (both real defensive-copy
      fixes, not exclusions): those had a real, provably-immutable alternative available
      (an interface with no mutating surface, or List.copyOf). No such alternative exists for a
      live ObjectMapper/Redis client or for a service class that depends on one.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Or>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.cache.ShortLinkCache"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.service.ShortLinkService"/>
            <Class name="com.artmendez.urlshortener.v2.shortlink.web.ShortLinkController"/>
        </Or>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
